## Critical Rules

### Build and Testing
- **ALWAYS build before commit**: `npm run build` must succeed
- **ALWAYS test changes**: Ensure functionality works as expected
- **NO partial implementations**: Complete features atomically
- **NO breaking changes**: Maintain backward compatibility

### Code Standards
- Follow `.ai/rules/code-style.mdc` for all code
- Follow `.ai/rules/discord-bot-patterns.mdc` for Discord.js patterns
- Maintain type safety - no `any` types
- Keep functions focused and small
- Document complex logic

### Git and Version Control
- **Never commit directly** unless explicitly asked
- Keep commits focused and atomic
- Write clear commit messages explaining WHY
- Test thoroughly before marking complete
- Follow conventional commit format when appropriate

### Documentation Standards
- Keep README.md up to date with features
- Document complex algorithms inline
- Update environment variable documentation
- Maintain clear function signatures

## Discord Bot Development Patterns

### Command Structure
- Each command in its own file under `src/commands/`
- Export SlashCommandBuilder as `data`
- Export async `execute` function
- Handle all interaction states (deferred, replied, etc.)

### Error Handling
- Wrap command execution in try/catch
- Log errors with context
- Provide user-friendly error messages
- Use ephemeral messages for errors

### State Management
- Use globalThis for bot-wide state
- Initialize with fallback pattern
- Clear state appropriately
- Document global declarations

## Scraping Best Practices
- Rotate user agents to avoid blocking
- Handle parsing errors gracefully
- Validate data before storage
- Log scraping failures with context

## Notification System
- Parse dates correctly with timezone handling
- Group events by time
- Schedule with proper delay calculation
- Clean up old timeouts
- Update notifications with fresh data

## Environment Variables
Required variables in `.env`:
- `DISCORD_TOKEN`: Bot authentication token
- `DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID`: Target channel for notifications
- `CLIENT_ID`: Discord application client ID
- `FAKE_DATE`: (Optional) For testing date-based features
- `RESCRAPE`: (Optional) Force data update on startup

## Task Completion Requirements
- **Complete ALL tasks**: Build, test, verify, and update docs
- **Zero errors**: Fix all TypeScript and runtime errors
- **Update tracking**: Mark todos complete only when fully done
- **Return to user**: Only when 100% complete and verified

## Work Continuation Philosophy
- **Continue work systematically**: Complete comprehensive changes
- **No incremental stopping**: Finish entire cleanup/refactor sessions
- **Work through all files**: Don't stop after minimal changes
- **Focus on completion**: Comprehensive improvements over partial fixes

## Debug and Troubleshooting
- Check Discord API status if bot issues occur
- Verify environment variables are set correctly
- Test scraping URLs for changes in HTML structure
- Monitor rate limits and API quotas
- Review logs for error patterns
